That sounds like it could be Mine's End.

There are three versions of Mine's End.

In the most common version, the up stair is near the
middle of the northern portion, and there are several
secret doors with mimics and gems behind them.
The other two versions cannot be mistaken, because
they look significantly different from a normal Gnomish
Mines cavern level.

In any case, find all the gray stones on the level,
kick-test them (while NOT wearing gauntlets of
power), and pick up any that move when kicked.
If there's more than one, you can price-check
them when you get back up to Minetown, to
find out which one is the luckstone.  Also, use
the altar there to BUC-check it.  Once you have
access to a co-aligned altar (or holy water from
any other source), you'll bless the luckstone,
your bag of holding if you have one, and as
many scrolls of identify as you can lay your
hands on.

> Is Sokoban the only way to continue now?

You could also continue in the main dungeon,
but doing Sokoban as soon as you can is safer
(provided you don't flub it and run up a bunch
of luck penalties) and significantly more
beneficial.

Exception:  if you don't have an unlocking
device yet, you may want to hold off on the
zoo at the end of the fourth Sokoban level
until you get one.  Kicking down that door
can be fairly dangerous, as it tends to wake
up everything at once.

Also, in the rare event that Sokoban happens
to contain an abnormally dangerous monster
(or, somewhat more likely, a monster zapping
a particularly dangerous attack wand), that
would be a good reason to save it for later.

Nymphs in particular are much less dangerous
in Sokoban than most other places -- unless
they get hold of a dangerous wand.


